cial services, however she refused. Therefore, you need to respect her decision of not allowing disclosure, even if you consider this decision to be unwise.\n- Note - Ifyou suspect any patient who doesn't have capacity, after performing mental capacity assessment and you found he/she lacks capacity, then social services or appropriate authority should be involved. 38 / 90\n\n#### Clinical Scenario 38:\nA 54-year-old male presented to the ED With 6 weeks history of short of breath associated with dry cough and fever. You order covid PCR which is negative. His chest x-ray is shown. What would be your step of management in this patient?\n- **A)** Oseltamivir\n- **B)** Furosemide\n- **C)** IV co-amoxiclav *clarithromycin\n- **D)** Amoxicillin   E' Co-trimoxazole Explanation\n- Patient clinical features: dry cough and fever with negative covid PCR and X-ray finding: diffuse, patchy interstitial and alveolar infiltrates bilaterally are suggestive of Pneumocystis https\n- ]/mrcemexpert.com/courses/mrcem-intermediate-sba-diet-111esson/paper-i-2-2/\n\n23/11/2025, paper -l I MRCEM EXPERT LLC jirovecii(previously Pneumocystis carinii) pneumonla.\n- Management-of-pneumocystisjicue.cii\n- Co-trimoxazole in high dose. If patient can't tolerate then Atovaquone or choose unlicensed drugs (Combination of dapsone with trimethoprim OR clindamycin and primaquine).\n- Co-trimoxazole in high dosage. If patient can't tolerate then Pentamidine isetionate given by intravenous infusion\n- Adjungtiye#erapy\n- In moderate to severe infections associated with HIV infection, prednisolone is given by mouth for 5 days (alternatively, hydrocortisone may be given parenterally); the dose is then reduced to complete 21 days of treatment.\n- Prophylaxis\n- Co-trimoxazole by mouth is the drug of choice for prophylaxis against pneumocystis pneumonia. If patient can't tolerate Co-trimoxazole then Inhaled pentamidine isethionate. 39 / 90\n\n#### Clinical Scenario 39:\nA mother presents with an 18hours old 