 On\n- Inyestigations Schistosoma haematobium Can lead to o' (painless hematuria)\n- hyperten Son\n- pelvic\n- Schistosomiasis is diagnosed through the detection of parasite eggs in stool or urine specimens\n- Antibodies and/or antigens detected in blood or urine samples are also indications of infection.\n- FBC - normocytic, normochromic mild anemia often present; eosinophilia, occasionally thrombocytopenia\n- Urinalysis\n- Consider LET, renal function test , abdominal ultrasounds .\n- praziquantel\n- Consider anti-histamine and corticosteroid for dermatitis or reduce the severity of symptoms 19 / 90\n\n#### Clinical Scenario 19:\nA 29 year old man presents following a collapse. He is cyanosed, tachycardic and has Sp02 of 88% despite high- flow oxygen and a respiratory rate of 26 breaths per minute. He admits to recent recreational drug use. httpsumrcemexpert.com/courses/mrcem-intermediate-sba-diet-111esson/paper-ii-2-2/\n\n25/11/2025, 10:17 paper - II I MRCEM EXPERT LLC Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?\n- **A)** CNS depression and hypoventilation from opiates\n- **B)** Hypoxia secondary to Gamma Hydroxy Butyrate ingestion\n- **C)** Methaemoglobinaemia from amyl nitrate use\n- **D)** pulmonary vasoconstriction from cannabis smoking\n- **E)** Pulmonary vasoconstriction from cannabis smoking Explanation\n- Consider Methaemoglobinaemia diagnosis in any patient with cyanosis and hypoxia that doesn't respond to oxygen administration. httpsumrcemexpert.com/courses/mrcem-intermediate-sba-diet-111esson/paper-ii-2-2/\n\n25/11/2025, 10:17 paper - II I MRCEM EXPERT LLC 21 / 90\n\n#### Clinical Scenario 21:\nA 32-year-old male presented to the ED with complaint of painless bleeding. He states that he has found fresh\n\n25/11/2025, 10:17 paper - II I MRCEM EXPERT LLC bright red blood on the toilet paper. What is the most likely diagnosis ?\n- **A)** Peptic ulcer disease\n- **B)** Hemorrhoids\n- **C)** Irritable bowel syndrome\n- **D)** Anal fissure\n- **E)**